<title>UK: P&amp;O sells oilfield services for 37.5 mln stg.</title>
<headline>P&amp;O sells oilfield services for 37.5 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Peninsular and Oriental Steam Naviation Co said on Tuesday it has sold its wholly-owned subsidiary P&amp;O Oilfield Services Limited to a management buyout team and Royal Bank Development Management Ltd for 37.5 million stg.  </p>
<p>In a statement, the transport group said the sale will result in a profit of around 24.5 million stg compared with the unit's book value.</p>
<p>Aberdeen-based P&amp;O Oilfield Services rents equipment for drilling oil and gas wells in the North Sea and internationally.</p>
</text>
